you won't find standard flavors here  Pietro Samoa is colognes most creative  ice-cream maker he offers a wide variety  of unusual flavors like his newest  creation coconut sweet potato with  yogurt he got the idea one night during  dinner it's very sweet and the customers  seem to like it  Samara makes all his ice cream himself  today's featured flavor is mango one of  the most popular items on the menu here  at is gelateria the mangos are grown  organically and imported directly from  India when the ices the final product  has a very strong mango flavor and the  aroma of mangos it's great the mix of  fruit water sugar and a gelling agent is  stirred until it reaches the correct  consistency that usually takes about  seven minutes the Coco used here comes  from Virunga National Park in the  Democratic Republic of Congo some of the  proceeds are donated to the park we use  Coco from nature and then we give  something back to nature it's a  beautiful concept samuri seeks to uphold  the highest possible quality control  standards both for his ingredients and  the production of his ice cream his cafe  is located in the trendy part of  southern Cologne  he's been selling ice cream here for  four years he's always coming up with  new flavors always something different  right now my two favorites a mango and  passionfruit and if you like you can  order an espresso made with beans  roasted by another small Italian  business Pietro his wife helps him run  the cafe Pietro is a real perfectionist  and at first that was tough but I think  his perfectionism is partly what's made  us so successful you can see it in the  quality of our product Pietro Samaras  ice cream shop  another reason to visit Cologne  especially in the summertime
 

